---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SystemPlate from '../components/SystemPlate.astro';
import AgentSandboxDemo from '../components/AgentSandboxDemo.astro';
---

<Layout title="Work & Architecture" description="Architectural dossiers of platforms, identity systems, and agent sandboxes by Viswaroop Vadlamudi.">
  <div class="py-6 md:py-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Architectural Dossiers</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold font-heading text-[var(--text-primary)] mt-1 mb-3">Under the Surface</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-[var(--text-secondary)] max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        System diagrams show the connections. These dossiers explain the decisions, failure modes, and tradeoffs underneath them.
      </p>

      <!-- Jump Index -->
      <nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-6 font-mono text-xs" aria-label="Jump to a system">
        <a href="#multi-cloud" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] hover:border-[var(--border-hover)] hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-all">01 · Multi-Cloud Delivery ↘</a>
        <a href="#identity" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] hover:border-[var(--border-hover)] hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-all">02 · Owning Identity ↘</a>
        <a href="#reliability" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] hover:border-[var(--border-hover)] hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-all">03 · Reliability Loops ↘</a>
        <a href="#agents" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] hover:border-[var(--border-hover)] hover:text-[var(--accent)] transition-all">04 · Agent Sandboxes ↘</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-16">
      <!-- Dossier 1: Multi-Cloud -->
      <section class="craft-card p-6 md:p-8" id="multi-cloud">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4 pb-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">SYS—001 · Platform Engineering</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-heading mt-1">Different Clouds. One Way to Ship.</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Argo CD / EKS / GKE</span>
        </div>

        <div class="my-6 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] overflow-hidden bg-[var(--bg-canvas)] p-4">
          <SystemPlate kind="platform" />
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 my-6 text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Friction</h3>
            <p>More teams meant more deployment scripts, console changes, and coordination friction. The platform needed a delivery contract that stayed consistent as it scaled across clouds.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Approach</h3>
            <p>I designed a multi-tenant GitOps platform across EKS and GKE, with tenant resource quotas, network isolation policies, and automated risk-aligned promotion pipelines.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--accent)] pl-4">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Core Takeaway</h3>
            <p class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Standardize the delivery contract. Keep the cloud-specific tradeoffs explicit.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)] flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono">
          <span class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">Stack: Argo CD, Kustomize, Helm, Prometheus</span>
          <a href="/blog/2025-12-22-argo-cd-vs-flux-in-production/" class="text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">Read field note: Argo CD vs Flux in Production ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Dossier 2: Identity -->
      <section class="craft-card p-6 md:p-8" id="identity">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4 pb-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">SYS—002 · Identity & Tenancy</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-heading mt-1">Own the Boundary. Not Just the Login.</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] text-[var(--text-muted)]">ORY Hydra / Kratos / Keto</span>
        </div>

        <div class="my-6 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] overflow-hidden bg-[var(--bg-canvas)] p-4">
          <SystemPlate kind="identity" />
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 my-6 text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Friction</h3>
            <p>B2B multi-tenancy, enterprise SSO, and fine-grained permissions were pushing far beyond the limits and lock-in of managed Cognito setups.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Approach</h3>
            <p>Led the migration to open-source IAM: separating human authentication (Kratos), OAuth2 token issuance (Hydra), and relationship-based authorization (Keto).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--accent)] pl-4">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Core Takeaway</h3>
            <p class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Cost and lock-in tradeoffs must be made explicit before you're three years in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)] flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono">
          <span class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">Stack: ORY Hydra, Kratos, Keto, OAuth2/OIDC</span>
          <a href="/blog/2025-12-21-identity-platforms-fail-at-the-frontend-boundary-part-1-the-boundary-problem/" class="text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">Read field note: Identity at the Frontend Boundary ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Dossier 3: Reliability -->
      <section class="craft-card p-6 md:p-8" id="reliability">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4 pb-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">SYS—003 · Reliability & Operations</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-heading mt-1">Make the Safe Path the Obvious One.</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] text-[var(--text-muted)]">OPA / SLOs / Observability</span>
        </div>

        <div class="my-6 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-subtle)] overflow-hidden bg-[var(--bg-canvas)] p-4">
          <SystemPlate kind="reliability" />
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 my-6 text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Friction</h3>
            <p>Manual review gates created friction and delays, while operational expectations remained disconnected from daily development velocity.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Approach</h3>
            <p>Embedded pre-flight policy checks in CI, co-owned SLOs and runbooks with product squads, and recorded architectural tradeoffs in ADRs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--accent)] pl-4">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1 font-bold">The Core Takeaway</h3>
            <p class="font-heading text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Guardrails beat gates. Teams self-serve when the golden path is obvious.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)] flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono">
          <span class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">Stack: OpenSearch, Dynatrace, OPA Gatekeeper</span>
          <a href="/blog/2026-01-10-observability-on-aws-at-scale-six-years-of-lessons-from-opensearch-eks-and-production-reality/" class="text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">Read field note: 6 Years of Observability Lessons ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Dossier 4: Agent Sandboxes -->
      <section class="craft-card p-6 md:p-8" id="agents">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4 pb-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--accent)] uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">WIP—004 · Agentic Infrastructure</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-heading mt-1">What if the Caller Isn't a Person?</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--tag-bg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Zanzibar / MicroVMs / eBPF</span>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] mb-6 leading-relaxed">
          Autonomous AI agents act on behalf of users asynchronously for hours at a time. Traditional interactive browser-based OAuth2 redirects fail. Here is how zero-trust execution sandboxes, ephemeral M2M tokens, and relationship checks enforce blast-radius containment:
        </p>

        <AgentSandboxDemo />

        <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)] flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono">
          <span class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">Focus: M2M tokens, Firecracker/gVisor sandboxes</span>
          <a href="/blog/2026-03-28-why-ai-agents-will-break-your-identity-platform/" class="text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">Read deep dive: Why AI Agents Will Break Your Identity Platform ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
